out that fight they need  to specify a specific part of it  be it the under water Kamehameha the  times xx kaio-ken prisons death the  Super Saiyan transformation Frieza  getting cut in half go whose mercy  freezes death believe it or not I  skipped a ton of things from that fight  my point is that they are all  self-contained stories within a greater  narrative they were smaller battles  within a war the Goku beerus fight is no  different it begins with the  transformation it has Goku coming to  terms with his power and new abilities  Goku trying to land a clean shot and  beerus beerus and go who's hand clashes  go to chess getting stabbed and so on  all of these help build the story to a  final conclusion that is both thrilling  and satisfied the viewer we see beerus  early in this series and learn how he  operates by seeing him worked as a guard  destruction we begin to understand  weaves as a character more and the role  he plays in all of this the movie  however doesn't demonstrate bears as a  threat prior to his interaction with  goku it doesn't show him acting as a god  of destruction it has a fight that while  incredible is made of two parts and is a  self-contained fight sequence with no  interim micro stories the core issue is  that one of the movie's provides a much  more rich animation visual experience it  delivers a shallow representation of  what Dragon Ball fans have come to  appreciate and in reality it never some  chance with the extended runtime at 105  minutes compared to the animes 252  minutes for the air it was forced to cut  corners where it simply couldn't afford  to which means the deciding point has to  go to the anime the release the battle  of gods movie wasn't the wrong route  it was their only move it wasn't by  chance that the battle of gods movie was  the first continuation of the canon  since 1995 or ever with a movie the  truth is after almost two decades past  by Toei wasn't sure if the Japanese  public was still interested in  Dragonball the same way it was in the  early 90s and so they tested the  public's interest with this movie and in  reality it's thanks to the success of  battle of gods and resurrection of F  that we now have our old show back in  producing new content weekly and while I  know there are many of you out there who  resent Dragon Ball super and find it  boring or subpar  I can't change your mind but I will say  this the first saga of Dragon Ball Z had  39 episodes and I got us to this point  this is what happened on the 39th  episode of Dragon Ball super it's still  such a young show and has so much yet to  offer but I'd love to hear what you guys  think do you agree disagree let me know  in the comment section down below if you  guys want to see more Dragon Ball  content like this please feel free to  subscribe I'm totally not Marc  I'll until we meet again guys thank you  so much for watching
 

